# Expo normally gitignores `expo-env.d.ts` (auto-regenerated on every
# `expo install` / `expo start`), but CI needs its triple-slash type
# reference to resolve — without it `process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_*` degrades
# to `any` and trips `@typescript-eslint/no-unsafe-assignment`. Checking
# in the two-line file is a deliberate override of Expo's default.